  "messages": [
    {
      "content": "Solve this problem step by step. Put your final answer within \\boxed{}.\n\nWhat percentage younger is Nani's sister than Nani? Nani is 9 years old. Nani's sister is 20% younger than Nani.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Nani’s sister is stated to be **20% younger** than Nani.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{20\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "GOOD: —\nBAD: —\nWATCH: \"Solve this problem step by step. Put you\"",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Wait, I made a mistake. Nani is 8 years old.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Nani is now 8 years old. Her sister is still stated to be **20% younger**.\n\n\\[\n20\\%\\text{ of }8=0.2\\times 8=1.6\n\\]\n\nSo her sister is \\(8-1.6=6.4\\) years old, but the percentage difference remains:\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{20\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Actually, that was wrong. Nani's sister is 25% younger than Nani.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Nani’s sister is **25% younger** than Nani.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25\\%}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Oh, I forgot to mention: Nani's sister's age is compared with Nani's age using Nani's age as the reference.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Using Nani’s age as the reference:\n\n\\[\n\\frac{\\text{Nani's age}-\\text{sister's age}}{\\text{Nani's age}}\\times 100\\%\n=25\\%\n\\]\n\nSince Nani is 8, her sister would be:\n\n\\[\n8(1-0.25)=6\\text{ years old}\n\\]\n\nThus, the sister is\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{25\\%}\n\\]\n\nyounger than Nani.",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Great. Now let's take that a step further. How old will Nani be when her sister turns 10? Also, here's some relevant info: Nani's sister is currently 6 years old.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Nani is currently 8, and her sister is 6, so the age difference is:\n\n\\[\n8-6=2\\text{ years}\n\\]\n\nWhen her sister turns 10, Nani will still be 2 years older:\n\n\\[\n10+2=12\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12\\text{ years old}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Here's another detail: Nani and her sister will age by one year each year.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "Since both Nani and her sister age by one year each year, their **2-year age difference stays constant**.\n\n- Sister’s current age: \\(6\\)\n- Years until she turns 10: \\(10-6=4\\)\n- Nani’s age then: \\(8+4=12\\)\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{12\\text{ years old}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    },
    {
      "content": "Good, now using that, can you calculate: What is the total age of Nani, Nani's brother, and Nani's sister? By the way, Nani's brother is twice Nani's age.",
      "role": "user"
    },
    {
      "content": "- Nani: \\(8\\) years old  \n- Nani’s sister: \\(6\\) years old  \n- Nani’s brother: \\(2 \\times 8 = 16\\) years old  \n\nTotal age:\n\n\\[\n8+6+16=30\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{30\\text{ years}}\n\\]",
      "role": "assistant"
    }
  ],
